I will compute the number of applicants missing exactly one of the six selected criteria (excluding citizenship):
- Degree Level/Field: Degree Level in {Masters, PhD} AND Degree Field in {Biology, Biochemistry, Biotechnology}
- Experience >= 3
- Lab Trained == 'Y'
- Publications >= 3
- Programming Lang in {C++, C#, Fortran}
- Second Language is non-empty

Running the analysis now.

python
import pandas as pd

df = pd.read_excel('./jobdata/Applicants.xlsx')

valid_fields = {'Biology','Biochemistry','Biotechnology'}
valid_levels = {'Masters','PhD'}
valid_langs = {'C++','C#','Fortran'}

def missing_six(row):
    miss = 0
    if (row['Degree Level'] not in valid_levels) or (row['Degree Field'] not in valid_fields):
        miss += 1
    if pd.isna(row['Experience (Years)']) or row['Experience (Years)'] < 3:
        miss += 1
    if str(row['Lab Trained (Y/N)']).strip().upper() != 'Y':
        miss += 1
    if pd.isna(row['Publications']) or row['Publications'] < 3:
        miss += 1
    if str(row['Programming Lang']).strip() not in valid_langs:
        miss += 1
    if pd.isna(row['Second Language']) or str(row['Second Language']).strip() == '':
        miss += 1
    return miss

six_miss = df.apply(missing_six, axis=1)
count_exactly_one = int((six_miss == 1).sum())
print(f"Number of applicants missing exactly one qualification (excluding citizenship): {count_exactly_one}")
